f Plan Approval:   July 9, 2024, Council Meeting - Motion 154/2024  Time Frame of Plan:   2024 - 2028  Key Concepts of the Plan:     Shared vision that represents elected officials, municipal employees, and community members. (community driven plan)     Actions can be prioritized annually with budget cycle and can be easily measured to understand performance     Plan evolved from a thorough review of key planning documents, a community survey and a public information session which was used to gather community perspective to develop the plan\n\nCouncil Workshops/Strategic Planning     April 17, 2024,   Community Survey posted regarding the development of a strategic plan. Survey remained open until April 26, 2024. 138 responses received.     May 1, 2024 , strategic planning session held with Mayor and Council and facilitated by Parkland Community Planning Services to review survey response feedback and establish long term goals and objectives.     June 19, 2024 , Mayor and Council along with administration hosted a public information session and engagement to share initial thoughts, goals and objectives for the new strategic plan. Members of the community that attended shared further feedback to shape a long-term vision for the community.     July 9, 2024 , final version of the Bentley Strategic Plan presented to council and was approved unanimously through motion 154/2024     After July 9, 2024   - Quarterly of status of goals and objectives and progress towards completion. This happens each year to ensure we stay on track.\n\nVision:  The Town of Bentley is a community offering a high quality of life, that is safe, clean, attractive, affordable and family oriented. Bentley celebrates community spirit where citizens are actively involved in shaping the future of the community as   “The Place to Be.” Our Core Values Community Centric:   We prioritize the needs and desires of our residents  Collaboration:   We work together with various stakeholders to achieve